                    <history>
                        <origin> <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notBefore="0700" notAfter="0799">s.
                            viii</origDate> </origin>
                        <provenance type="rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_190">Ely,
                            Cambridgeshire, Benedictine abbey and (1109) cathedral priory of St
                            Peter and St Etheldreda</orgName> <p>This attribution was accepted
                            (albeit with a query) in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                            Great Britain (1964). An explanation was provided in a footnote (p. 78,
                            n. 9): <q>Cotton Tib. B.v fo. 76 and Sloane 1044, fo. 2 are leaves from
                            Cambridge, U.L., Kk.1.24; Cotton Tib B.v fo. 74, containing Ely
                            documents, was probably originally a blank leaf of the same
                            volume.</q></p> <p>The Ely attribution for MS Kk.1.24 (and dispersed
                            leaves) was later rejected in the Supplement (1987), for the following
                            reason (p. 35, n. 2): <q>CUL, Kk.1.24 contains Ramsey Abbey, not Ely,
                            documents</q>. Compare the following headnote for Ely, added in MLGB3
                            (2010-2015): <q>MLGB recorded Cambridge, UL MS Kk. 1. 24 (Evangelia, s.
                            viii) and dispersed leaves, now BL MSS Cotton Tib. B. v fols. 74 and 76,
                            and Sloane 1044 fol. 2, as possibly from Ely, since Tib. B. v fol. 74, a
                            once-blank flyleaf, has documents in English (s. x ex) that were thought
                            to relate to Ely; but this was rejected in the Supplement on the basis
                            that the documents related instead to Ramsey abbey.</q></p>
                        </provenance>
